# The three distance searches. Minutes of arithmetic, with a working Cancel.
#
#   find_min_aggr_single_round          ternary search over one round
#   find_min_aggregation_in_window      coarse sweep + refine, all rounds
#   find_distance_for_target_aggregation  282 probes, each recomputing 11 rounds
#
# The last one is why this is an action and not a service. Every probe recomputes
# all eleven rounds; driving that loop from the client would be 282 round trips
# carrying ~4 MB of table each way. As one job it is one call, and the operator
# can still stop it -- cancelling unwinds the search wherever it is and leaves the
# table at the last probe, which is exactly what the old progress dialog's Cancel
# did.
string op
string table_json
string params_json
---
bool success

# The table as the last probe left it, even on cancel.
string table_json

# {"best_distance": 312.5, "best_aggr": 0.084,
#  "samples": [[distance, aggregation], ...]}
# `samples` is what the search plot draws.
string result_json

# True when the operator cancelled. success is still true: a cancelled search
# produced a partial answer, it did not fail.
bool cancelled

string message
---
int32 done
int32 total       # 0 when the op cannot report a total -- show it indeterminate
string stage
